# .dockerignore — files Docker should NOT send to the build.
#
# Why it matters: `docker build .` first uploads the whole folder (the "build
# context") to the Docker engine. Ignoring junk here:
#   - makes builds faster (node_modules alone can be hundreds of MB),
#   - prevents your Mac/Windows node_modules from overwriting the Linux ones
#     the image installs itself (some packages contain OS-specific binaries),
#   - keeps secrets (.env) and local build output out of the image.

# Dependencies and build output — the image creates its own
node_modules
.next
out

# Version control and editor files
.git
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Secrets, logs and docs
.env*
npm-debug.log*
*.md

# The Dockerfile itself doesn't need to be inside the context
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
